:[{"text":"Tree placement"},{"text":"Shading"},{"text":"Drainage"},{"text":"Terrain"},{"text":"Circulation"},{"text":"Planting patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Nature-Based Solutions"},{"type":"p","text":"Future landscape architects will increasingly work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urban forests"},{"text":"Wetlands"},{"text":"Green roofs"},{"text":"Green walls"},{"text":"Bioswales"},{"text":"Rain gardens"},{"text":"Ecological corridors"},{"text":"Sponge-city systems"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Arch"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Landscape Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Site Planning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Planting Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Landscape Ecology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Grading & Drainage"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Stormwater Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Climate-Resilient Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Rhino / Grasshopper"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"3D Visualization"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Landscape Construction"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Urban Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Biodiversity Planning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Water-Sensitive Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Environmental Analysis"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Project Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Client Communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to take a landscape project through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Site Survey","Topography & GIS Analysis","Climate & Ecological Analysis","User & Program Analysis","Landscape Concept","Landform & Circulation","Planting Strategy","Water & Stormwater Strategy","Hardscape Design","Grading & Drainage","Landscape Construction Details","3D / Visualization","Planting & Material Documentation","Cost / Quantity Estimation","Site Coordination"]},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, aim for 3–5 landscape-focused projects, at least one GIS-based project, one climate-resilience or ecological project, relevant internship experience, and a portfolio showing both conceptual design and technical documentation."}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile for this career is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Landscape Design","Ecology","GIS","Site Engineering","Climate Resilience","Green Infrastructure","Digital Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The future-ready Landscape Architect should not be positioned simply as a designer of gardens and parks."},{"type":"p","text":"A stronger professional identity is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Landscape Architect","Ecological Designer","Climate-Resilience Specialist"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination opens pathways into urban landscape design, ecological restoration, green infrastructure, climate adaptation, public-realm development, sustainable urbanism, and large-scale environmental planning."}]}]}